CROSS-LAYER PROOF CHALLENGE inspired by FreeToken semantic-aware recurrent-state caching. Bonfyre already knows semantic boundaries (turns, tool calls, tool outputs, thinking/compaction boundaries, WorkOccurrences). Local/model realizations should be able to use those exact boundaries as performance-only checkpoint anchors.

Do not create a second conversation-memory truth. Add a SemanticCheckpointRef/representation-level anchor only if an existing owner can carry it:
semantic prefix identity + model/route/body identity + checkpoint position + state/KV representation + validity + evidence locality.

Required invariants:
- editing/pruning a tool output invalidates checkpoints after the edit but preserves the deepest exact surviving prefix;
- semantic boundary IDs come from canonical interaction structure, not tokenizer heuristics alone;
- restored recurrent/KV state changes realization cost only, never semantic meaning/authority;
- model/precision/runtime/toolchain changes invalidate incompatible checkpoints;
- compaction may remove raw payload while retaining digest/evidence sufficient to decide reuse;
- cache miss/cold start remains correct, merely slower.

Real-use proof should compare an agent turn sequence before/after a tool-output prune and show less re-prefill/recomputation with identical semantic result/evidence.
